 r←IsAvailableElsewhere report
⍝ Takes one of the matrices Tatin's `CheckForLaterVersion` returns and marks with a 1 exactly those
⍝ rows whose installed version is hosted by a Registry other than the one it was installed from:
⍝ [;2] repeats [;1], so there is nothing later, yet [;5] names a Registry.\\
⍝ That is what a package looks like that was installed from a local Registry before being published.
⍝ Re-installing it from the dependency list changes no version, it only corrects the URL the build
⍝ list records; see `ReInstallFromDependencies`.\\
⍝ Rows carrying one of Tatin's "<<< ... >>>" markers are ruled out by [;1]≢[;2] already.\\
⍝ See `IsUpdateCandidate` for the rows that do offer a later version.
 r←(report[;1]≡¨report[;2])∧0<≢¨report[;5]
⍝Done
